LANDING PR #422: ratchet function size, nesting, parameter lists and every lint suppression with #[expect], so the baseline can only shrink (issue #337).

Branch story-337-expect-ratchet: one commit, 90f98eda, on main 1d890c6a, from the operator's controller. It touches 94 files, 80 of them in a mechanical sweep. Changes:
- a root clippy.toml (100 lines, nesting 5, 7 parameters, as ruled into decision 0071 ruling 4), repeated in core's and view's clippy.toml;
- workspace lints: too_many_lines, struct/fn_params_excessive_bools, allow_attributes and allow_attributes_without_reason, dbg_macro, todo, unreachable_pub;
- every suppression converted to #[expect(..., reason)], with today's offenders on reason "baseline 2026-09, #288" (counts in quality/suppressions.txt);
- 223 unreachable pub items made pub(crate) by rustc's machine fix;
- 8 stale allows removed;
- multiple-versions = "deny" with a 7-entry skip list that may only shrink;
- crates/brokkr-cli/tests/suppressions.rs, a lexer count that must equal the baseline;
- a CI step refusing a new unruled production suppression;
- tests/support/test_paths.rs as the one home of the test-path vocabulary.

Judge:
1. Whether the sweep preserves behaviour: pub(crate) only where nothing outside the crate reaches, expects matching what clippy fires, no logic touched.
2. Whether every ratchet fails closed: a new suppression that evades the count or the CI refusal (a cfg_attr form, an inner #![expect], a multi-line attribute, a reason without a ruling), and a skip-list entry that can grow.
3. Whether the committed counts match the tree.

Threat model (operator ruling, 2026-09-26): catch realistic accidental misuse and fail closed on what cannot be read. Deliberate evasion is a low residual.

This run lands one pull request under decision 0051 so the contribution gate can vouch for it. If a finding returns the branch, fix exactly that finding, prove it with a test bound by a compiling mutation, commit one signed-off commit ending "Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>", and never push. Do not run scripts/coverage-exact.sh; the controller runs it.
